      <pattern name="entity-operations" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md">Create payload shapes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-13/FR-12/NFR-07; re-grep `OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` and every OwnedChildWrite symbol each caller uses.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check (UAC-r2 PR #2110, ontology-r1 PRs). Record the result and the sequencing in the task notes. Escalate if a PR rewrites ChildRecordEndpoints.CreateAsync or the decision cores.</step>
    <step order="2">Write failing tests first: chat-created child carries the I-1 stamp, I-16 and sharee mirror at create; route, chat and decision-follow-on creates of the same child under the same parent produce the same owner and stamp; each caller maps a refusal through the shared map.</step>
    <step order="3">Re-point the route create core, then the chat create handler, email.draft and budget inquiry. Move `ForPersonColumns` / "for" person handling into the service path (already registry-driven by task 012); delete the handlers' private WhoAmI and for-person code.</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm the decision cores: `DecisionRouteCores.CreateChildAsync` -> `ChildRecordEndpoints.CreateAsync` now reaches the service; add the parity test for `AddTodoExecutor` / `AssignWorkExecutor`. Edit the decision cores only if they still reference a removed symbol.</step>
    <step order="5">Remove the create half of `OwnedChildWrite` (leave `RefileAsync` and every symbol still referenced elsewhere). Compile; run RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (ledger unchanged), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, all Signals decision tests.</step>
    <step order="6">Publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a re-pointed caller's response contract (status code or `errorCode`) would change for an existing refusal, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 (breaking API contract); do not change the contract to fit the shared map.</trigger>
    <trigger>If /conflict-check shows UAC-r2 PR #2110 or an ontology-r1 PR edits the same lines of ChildRecordEndpoints.cs, OwnedChildWrite.cs or the decision cores, STOP and ask the human to sequence the work.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a chat tool must create a table that is not in RecordTableRules, STOP: add the table to the registry through task 012's pattern or escalate; never bypass the service.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `OwnedChildWrite.CreateAsync` in src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api: four call sites (ChildRecordEndpoints.cs ~:258, DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs ~:341, EmailDraftToolHandler.cs ~:455, BudgetInquiryExecutor.cs ~:242). Existing tests for chat creates: tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*.cs; none asserts the I-1 stamp on a chat-created child.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for production code: callers are re-pointed at the service from task 013, no new production file. The only new file is a test class because the SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests* suite must pass unchanged and cannot take new assertions.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Chat creates keep skipping the I-1 stamp, I-16 and sharee mirror, and the route, chat and decision creates keep two authorization cores whose owner and mapping behaviour drift (spec FR-13, section 11 table).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
    <tool name="skill:conflict-check">Detect overlap with UAC-r2 PR #2110 and ontology-r1</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ChildRecordEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/DataverseCreateRecordHandler.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Handlers/EmailDraftToolHandler.cs</output>
